From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dodaskot <pessdres@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:28:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 123/131] drm/panel: hx83112f: keep reset deasserted in deep
 standby by default

Driving RESX low after entering deep standby takes the controller out of
deep standby while IOVCC stays powered. The vendor driver leaves reset
high here. Nine same-boot 120 s suspend measurements on the A22 5G showed
lower suspend current with reset kept high in every comparison (mean
13.06 vs 14.04 mA, pair differences 0.17-1.60 mA). prepare() still
asserts reset before the rails come back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx83112f.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx83112f.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx83112f.c
index 09977fd9a..0bf1d9f79 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx83112f.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx83112f.c
@@ -249,7 +249,7 @@ static int hx83112f_disable(struct drm_panel *panel)
 	return 0;
 }
 
-static bool keep_reset_in_standby;
+static bool keep_reset_in_standby = true;
 module_param(keep_reset_in_standby, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(keep_reset_in_standby,
 		 "Leave reset deasserted after deep standby, as the vendor driver does");
